<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="fa" dir="rtl">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    @* The page's own text is the largest thing on screen, and it cannot be painted until this
       font arrives. Asking for it here rather than waiting for the stylesheet to be parsed and
       reach the @@font-face rule saves a whole round trip on a slow connection - which on an
       Iranian mobile network is not a rounding error. The path is the plain one on purpose: it
       has to match what the stylesheet asks for, or the browser fetches the font twice. *@
    <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="fonts/Vazirmatn-Regular.woff2" crossorigin />

    @* Assets[...] resolves to the fingerprinted name that MapStaticAssets publishes, which comes
       with a year-long immutable cache and a pre-compressed brotli copy. The name changes when
       the file does, so nobody is ever served a stale stylesheet - which has already cost us one
       debugging session.

       Bootstrap is deliberately not here. It is used by the scaffolded account pages and by
       nothing else on the site, so it now loads only inside AccountLayout: 163 KB of
       render-blocking CSS that every visitor to the front page used to download for nothing. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    @* Loaded last so the design system wins over the starter styles it replaces. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["digicard.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["DigiCard.Web.styles.css"]" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#365b4c" />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>

<body>
    <Routes />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
